# ===========================================================================
# CREST 3.0.2 - external-calculator gradient file reused across MTD workers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Symptom : every `*MTD n` finishes after ~12 s with "terminated EARLY",
#           then "**ERROR** empty ensemble file crest_dynamics.trj".
# Cause   : xtb_sc/orca_sc/turbom_sc cached the FULL gradient-file path in
#           calc%gradfile on the first (trial) call.  parallel.f90 swaps
#           calc%calcspace to calcspace//"_i" for every worker thread but
#           does NOT deallocate gradfile/efile, so all workers kept reading
#           the stale trial-MTD file.  rd_grad_engrad only validates n==nat,
#           never the coordinates, so the frozen gradient was accepted and
#           the MD integrated it until SHAKE failed.
# Fix     : re-derive the path from the CURRENT calc%calcspace on every call,
#           exactly like the (correct) generic_sc.f90 implementation.
#
# The same patch also completes the ORCA subprocess interface (orca_sc.f90):
# rd_ORCA_wbo() was an unimplemented stub that hard-errored whenever WBOs
# were requested from an ORCA calculation (reachable via -shake / NCI mode
# and the wbo/flexi tools).  It now parses ORCA's Mayer bond-order block
# from ORCA.out  (  B( 0-C , 1-S ) : 1.0550  ), converts the ZERO-based
# ORCA indices to CREST's one-based convention, symmetrises the matrix and
# warns (instead of aborting) when the block is absent.
#
# And it makes the ORCA template survive: subprocess_types.f90 declared
#   character(len=:),allocatable :: input(:)      ! deferred-length ARRAY
# A deferred-length character array COMPONENT is mis-copied when the
# derived type is assigned (gcc PR fortran/89200, a GCC 9 regression).
# The calculator settings are copied (tmpcalc = env%calc, calc%add()), so
# the stored template lines turned into heap garbage and CREST wrote a
# BINARY ORCA.in - NUL bytes plus fragments of its own banner and string
# table.  ORCA rejected it with "ERROR: non-ASCII character(s) found in
# words" and CREST reported only "Initial geometry optimization failed!".
# Fixed by making the element length fixed (character(len=orca_linelen)).
# NOTE: that fix is only half the job.  The allocation must be changed in
# the same step, otherwise you land in gcc PR fortran/113793: with
#   allocate(self%input(nlines),source=repeat(" ",width))   ! width ~85
# gfortran <= 13 silently sizes the elements by the SOURCE length instead
# of the declared one, every later assignment writes 1056 bytes into an
# ~85-byte element, and the next free() aborts with
#   "double free or corruption (out)" / SIGABRT in read_orca_input.
# Hence: allocate(self%input(nlines),source=repeat(" ",orca_linelen)).
# PR89200 and PR113793 must be fixed TOGETHER.
# orca_sc.f90 additionally captures ORCA's stderr into ORCA.err instead
# of discarding it with 2>/dev/null, so a start-up failure is visible.
# Apply   : git apply -p1 crest-xtbsys-mtd-fix.patch    (from the src/ parent)
# ===========================================================================
